    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Pay:</b> $40–$75/hr plus groceries</li><li><b>Startup:</b> $0–$100</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Skilled home cooks</li></ul>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="callout"><strong>Short-term rentals:</strong> Renting out your apartment for under 30 days is heavily restricted in NYC. Under the city's registration law, hosts must register, be present during the stay and host no more than two guests. Most Airbnb-style income plans don't work here.</div>

<h2 id="start-this-month">How to start a side hustle in New York this month</h2>
<ol class="steps">
  <li><strong>Match the hustle to your commute.</strong> Pick work you can do near home or work so you don't lose an hour on the train each way.</li>
  <li><strong>Set a target in dollars, not hours.</strong> Decide what you need per month and work backward. Our <a href="/tools/income-calculator/">income calculator</a> does the math.</li>
  <li><strong>Sign up for one app and one local channel.</strong> One platform (Rover, TaskRabbit, DoorDash) plus one community channel (building groups, Nextdoor, parent chats).</li>
  <li><strong>Get three reviews in two weeks.</strong> Discount your first jobs if needed. In a crowded market, reviews decide who gets booked.</li>
  <li><strong>Plan around the calendar.</strong> Mark September 1 move-ins, the US Open, UNGA week, the Marathon and the holidays.</li>
  <li><strong>Open a separate account and save for taxes.</strong> City plus state plus federal adds up fast.</li>
</ol>

<h2 id="nyc-taxes">New York State and NYC taxes on side income</h2>
<p>New York City has one of the heaviest tax loads in the country, so plan from day one:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>State income tax:</strong> graduated rates from just under 4% to 10.9% for very high earners. A small middle-class rate cut took effect for tax year 2026.</li>
  <li><strong>NYC income tax:</strong> residents pay roughly 3.078% to 3.876% on top of state tax.</li>
  <li><strong>Self-employment tax:</strong> 15.3% federal on net profit. Use the <a href="/tools/self-employment-tax-calculator/">self-employment tax calculator</a> to estimate.</li>
  <li><strong>Unincorporated Business Tax:</strong> if your gross business income exceeds $95,000, you must file a city UBT return. Exemptions and credits often reduce small filers' bills.</li>
  <li><strong>MCTMT:</strong> self-employed people in the five boroughs owe the transit mobility tax only when net earnings exceed $150,000 (from 2026), at 0.60%.</li>
  <li><strong>Sales tax:</strong> if you sell goods, register for a Certificate of Authority. Combined NYC sales tax is 8.875%.</li>
</ul>
<p>Expect 1099-K or 1099-NEC forms from apps and clients, and track expenses like phone, supplies, bike maintenance and transit used for work.</p>

